data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Centre the series once: d = x - mean(x). The denominator is the dot product of d with itself, over all n\nvalues. The lag-k numerator is the dot product of d[0 : n - k] with d[k : n], which has n - k products. Divide\nit by the same denominator, not by n - k. Entry 0 then comes out as exactly 1."},"hints_note":null}

